    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both parties: this ruling concerns trip TRP-00502 only.\n\nTHE MEASUREMENT. POL-RD-01 requires the threshold test on gps_trace.trace_distance_km, not the rounded 8.8 km convenience copy on the trip record. The trace records 8.77 km against a booked optimal route of 5.60 km. The excess is 3.17 km, or 56.6% of the optimal route: both establishment tests pass (over 20% and over 0.8 km), and the 50% mark is crossed, so the deviation is also MATERIAL. The trace carries no defect for policy purposes (100% coverage, 145 fixes, 10-second cadence, no gaps), so no POL-RD-07(a)-(c) impairment arises and the rider's burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry TRP-00502 and their timestamps agree.\n\nTHE DRIVER'S EXPLANATION. The bundle contains no traffic advisory for this trip: EV-ADVIS-00502-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, with no payload. Under POL-RD-13 the driver's account of 'a road works sign near Telok Blangah' is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else; with no advisory on file, POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the account carries no weight under POL-RD-08 and reduces no kilometre of the excess. The chat log is empty (0 messages), so POL-RD-04 gives no reduction; no amendment marker exists under POL-RD-05; and the vehicle was RYDE_PLUS, not a pooled trip under POL-RD-12.\n\nTHE MONEY, LINE BY LINE. POL-RD-02 recomputes the fare on the booked optimal route: (3.80 base + 0.75 x 5.60 km + 0.28 x 9.0 min) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the 0.80 platform fee = 11.32. charged_total 17.92 less recomputed_fare 11.32 = 6.60. That is 36.8% of the charge, below the 90% at which POL-RD-02 would itself convert to a full refund, and well above the 0.50 de minimis floor. No ERP, toll or surcharge line exists to be added or carved out (off-optimal-route ERP total 0.00; the trip did not originate at an airport), so nothing is added on top of, or subtracted from, that figure under POL-RD-09.\n\nTHE UPLIFT. A MATERIAL deviation makes the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check mandatory. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 4, which is 3 or more, so a repeat deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED on the clause-named field; the lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and is not used. The deviation is MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own trace, so POL-RD-06(b) applies and the remedy becomes FULL_REFUND of the whole charged_total rather than the POL-RD-02 partial. Printed side by side as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 figure 6.60; uplifted figure 17.92. There are no government-set or third-party pass-through lines to exclude from the uplift.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT GRANT. The rider asks for refunds on three earlier rides and for an examination of the driver's history. No artifact in this bundle describes any other trip, and an assertion citing no evidence ID carries no weight under POL-RD-08, so nothing beyond the 17.92 charged for TRP-00502 can be decided on this file; the history question is answered by the referral below, not by money. The driver's advocate argued the POL-RD-06(b) uplift is discretionary; the clause states the three effects that follow once the pattern is established, and the conditions for limb (b) are met, so the uplift is applied.\n\nWHY THIS IS NOT AN ESCALATION. POL-RD-10 was checked and no trigger fires. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07, the trip identifiers and timestamps match, no charge line lacks a counterpart in the trace or trip record, and the refund is 17.92, inside the ordinary limits. The missing advisory is not trigger (5): the driver cited no advisory identifier, and an assertion that cites no artifact cannot be invoked against one (POL-RD-13(1)). The absent advisory of weight 0.0 carries no fact and its absence is itself citable; every artifact that carries a deciding fact here carries weight 1.0, which is the cap on confidence under POL-GEN-02(2).\n\nFOR THE DRIVER: the referral to driver-conduct review under POL-RD-06(c) is a review of conduct, not a finding that this trip's measurement is wrong; the measurement rests on your own device telemetry. FOR THE RIDER: you are refunded the full 17.92 charged on TRP-00502."
  },
