    "explanation": "To the rider: your claim about this ride is upheld in full, and SGD 17.92 is refunded to you. To the driver: this finding rests on your own vehicle's GPS trace, not on the rider's impression, and the absent traffic record is not held against you — it simply cannot excuse the route.\n\nRoute (POL-RD-01). The governing length is the GPS trace EV-GPS-00502 at 8.77 km (trace_distance_km); the trip record's 8.8 km is a rounded convenience copy and was not used for the threshold test. Against the booked optimal of 5.60 km (EV-TRIP-00502) the excess is 3.17 km, or 56.6% of the optimal route. Both establishment tests pass (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED; because the excess also exceeds 50% it is MATERIAL, which makes the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check mandatory. Trace integrity (POL-RD-07): EV-GPS-00502 is unimpaired for policy purposes — 100% coverage, 145 fixes, a 10-second cadence equal to the expected interval, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0 — so none of limbs (a) to (c) fires and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises.\n\nThe driver's road-works explanation. Your statement says a road-works sign near Telok Blangah led you to take the hill road. The only traffic artifact in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00502-01, is MISSING — status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload — and a weight of 0.0 carries no fact. POL-RD-13 requires an external-traffic excuse to be tested against this trip's traffic advisory and nothing else; with no advisory on file POL-RD-03 cannot run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because no advisory identifier was named, the missing record is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) does not escalate this case. The gap does not aggravate your position either: the finding is made on the trace, not on the gap.\n\nNothing else reduces the excess. EV-CHAT-00502 is empty (0 messages), so there is no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 and no waypoint to test. The trip record shows no pickup or dropoff amendment and no amended optimal, so POL-RD-05 does not apply. The vehicle type is RYDE_PLUS, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The fare breakdown itemises no ERP, toll or surcharge lines (off-optimal-route ERP SGD 0.00; the trip did not originate at an airport), so POL-RD-09 neither adds nor subtracts anything and there is no billing-integrity correction to make.\n\nMoney (POL-RD-02). charged_total = SGD 17.92 (EV-FARE-00502). recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 5.60 km + 0.28 x 9.0 min) x the surge multiplier 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP + 0 surcharges - 0 promo = SGD 11.32. Refund = 17.92 - 11.32 = SGD 6.60. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and 36.8% of charged_total, below the 90% share that would convert a partial into a full refund, so on POL-RD-02 alone the outcome would be a partial refund.\n\nThe uplift (POL-RD-06). driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 4, which is 3 or more, so a repeat-deviation pattern is ESTABLISHED on the field the clause names; prior_deviation_flags (6) is a lifetime counter, is context only under POL-GEN-01, and was not used. The deviation is MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own evidence. The driver argues that limb (b) is discretionary and should not be exercised. I do not accept that: POL-RD-06 provides that where a pattern is established 'only these three effects follow', and (b) substitutes FULL_REFUND of charged_total for the POL-RD-02 partial. Both figures side by side, as the clause requires: POL-RD-02 partial = SGD 6.60; uplifted full refund = SGD 17.92 (the whole charged_total). No government-set or third-party pass-through line is carved out because there are none. You therefore pay nothing for this ride, and SGD 17.92 is refunded.\n\nReferral (POL-RD-06(c)). The pattern additionally requires the case to be referred to driver-conduct review. That is a referral, not an escalation: it does not displace or delay the refund.\n\nEarlier rides. You asked for refunds on three earlier rides and for the driver's history to be examined. No artifact in this bundle describes any trip but TRP-00502, so those claims cannot be assessed on this file and the contested amount here is SGD 17.92. The repeat-pattern finding was made only on the clause-named 90-day counter and goes to conduct review; if you hold details of specific earlier trips, they should be filed separately.\n\nConfidence is 0.90. The deciding facts — the trace, the booked optimal distance and the fare lines — all sit on artifacts at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02 cap is 1.0; the driver_profile carrying the pattern is likewise at 1.0."
  },
