    "explanation": "Both parties: the trip is TRP-00502, contested amount SGD 17.92. The case is decided on this trip's own measurements.\n\nDeviation (POL-RD-01). The governing length is the GPS trace, which POL-RD-01 makes authoritative where it disagrees with the rounded trip-record copy. The trace records 8.77 km (EV-GPS-00502) against a booked optimal of 5.60 km (EV-TRIP-00502) — an excess of 3.17 km, or 56.6%. Both establishment tests pass (56.6% > 20% and 3.17 km > 0.8 km), and 56.6% also crosses the 50% materiality band, so this is additionally a MATERIAL deviation. The rider discharged her initial burden under POL-RD-08: trip id TRP-00502 matches across trip record, trace and fare breakdown, and the start timestamp matches the first fix.\n\nNo reduction or exoneration applies. There is no chat-based detour request (POL-RD-04): the chat log EV-CHAT-00502 is empty, message_count 0, so no waypoint_hint exists and that test cannot be run. No pickup/dropoff amendment (POL-RD-05): all amendment fields are null. Not a pooled trip (POL-RD-12): vehicle_type is RYDE_PLUS, so the solo optimal of 5.60 km is the correct baseline. The driver's assertion of road works near Telok Blangah is tested against the traffic advisory for this trip and nothing else (POL-RD-13); the only advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00502-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver cites no advisory identifier, this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and it does not trigger escalation under POL-RD-10(5). The trace itself is unimpaired for policy purposes (100% coverage, no gaps, 10 s sampling), so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) do not fire, and no escalation trigger in POL-RD-10 applies.\n\nThe money. POL-RD-02 arithmetic: recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 × 5.60 km + 0.28 × 9.0 min) × 1.0 surge (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier; the trip record does not carry the field) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP + 0 surcharges + 0 waiting − 0 promo = 11.32. Refund = charged_total 17.92 − 11.32 = 6.60, which is 36.8% of the charge, so the POL-RD-02 baseline is a partial refund of 6.60. POL-RD-09 adds nothing: ERP and tolls are 0.00 with no gantry lines and no airport surcharge, so there is no pass-through correction either way.\n\nThe uplift. POL-RD-06's pattern test is met on the clause-named field alone — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 4. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags (6) is a deliberate near-synonym and is context only under POL-GEN-01; it is not relied on. Because the pattern is established and this deviation is both MATERIAL and substantiated on this trip's own trace, POL-RD-06(b) licenses FULL_REFUND of charged_total rather than the POL-RD-02 partial. Printed side by side as the clause requires: the POL-RD-02 figure is SGD 6.60; the uplifted figure is SGD 17.92, the whole charged_total. The only carve-out — government-set and third-party pass-through lines under POL-RD-09 — is empty here (ERP 0.00, no properly chargeable airport surcharge; the trip originates at Sentosa Gateway). The driver's contention that POL-RD-06(b) is discretionary is rejected: the clause states that where the pattern is established and the deviation is material and substantiated, the effect follows, and both conditions are met. The driver's point that the excess is far under the 8.0 km absolute band does not help, because POL-RD-01's materiality band is disjunctive and the 50% limb is crossed.\n\nOn the rider's request for refunds on three earlier rides: no artifact in the bundle describes any other trip. The contested amount on this file is the SGD 17.92 charged for TRP-00502 and nothing beyond it. The driver's conduct history is addressed where the policy puts it — the POL-RD-06(c) referral above, not as an adverse finding about this trip.\n\nConfidence: the deciding facts are carried by the trace, trip record, fare breakdown and driver profile, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the cap is 1.0. The MISSING advisory at 0.0 carries no deciding fact and does not lower the cap. Ruling FULL_REFUND of SGD 17.92."
